<article class="env-lemma" id="02GC">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02GC">Lemma <span data-tag="02GC">29.36.8</span>.</a> A closed immersion $i : Z \to X$ is unramified. It is G-unramified if and only if the associated quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals $\mathcal{I} = \mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(\mathcal{O}_ X \to i_*\mathcal{O}_ Z)$ is of finite type (as an $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module). </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/01TV" data-tag="01TV">29.22.7</a> and Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00UV" data-tag="00UV">10.151.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>